{title: House of the Rising Sun}
{artist: traditional}
{key: Am}
{tempo: 76}
{time: 6/8}
{x_license: public-domain}
{x_source: traditional American folk ballad}
{x_lang: en}
{x_difficulty: medium}
{x_scroll: 9}

{comment: Arpeggiate 6/8 throughout — three notes per beat}

{start_of_verse: 1}
There [Am]is a [C]house in [D]New Or[F]leans
They [Am]call the [C]Rising [E7]Sun
And it's [Am]been the [C]ruin of [D]many a poor [F]boy
And [Am]God, I [E7]know I'm [Am]one
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
My [Am]mother [C]was a [D]tailor [F]
She [Am]sewed my [C]new blue [E7]jeans
My [Am]father [C]was a [D]gamblin' [F]man
Down [Am]in New [E7]Or[Am]leans
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Oh [Am]mother, [C]tell your [D]child[F]ren
Not to [Am]do what [C]I have [E7]done
Spend your [Am]lives in [C]sin and [D]mise[F]ry
In the [Am]House of the [E7]Rising [Am]Sun
{end_of_chorus}
